# V2 analytic review: strict comparison covariance extension

Candidate reviewed in full:

    /home/chirurgie/.cache/q3-schur-anchor-analytic-v2-20260914.md
    SHA256 020297dd20f9184f6409055a6eff2c76ee257fbe7700fa81f9d81f165f0da3be

The v1 findings above are preserved. This section reviews only the new
candidate section 5 (candidate lines 86--118). It is a substantive extension
and is recorded separately.

## V2 pass 1: analytic audit

### Leading full-series reduction -- verified

The pinned source has

    Phi_ours(u)=2 Phi_C(u/2)
      = 4 pi^2 exp(9u/2) sum_(n>=1)
          [n^4-d n^2 exp(-2u)] exp[-pi n^2 exp(2u)],
    d=3/(2pi).

Separating n=1 and putting z=exp(2u) gives exactly the candidate's expression

    f(u)=(4pi^2/A) exp(9u/2) exp(-pi z)
          [1-d/z+E(z)],
    E(z)=sum_(n>=2) (n^4-d n^2/z) exp[-pi(n^2-1)z].

For z>=1, n^2-1>=3 for n>=2; after taking out exp(-3pi z),
the remaining polynomial-weighted Gaussian series is dominated by its z=1
series. Hence E(z)=O(exp(-3pi z)). This is a genuine control of the whole
tail, not a one-term heuristic and not a numerical premise.

### Asymptotic independence -- verified

For x<y in J, the two leading expressions give

    f(t+y)/f(t+x)
      = exp[9(y-x)/2-pi(exp(2y)-exp(2x))exp(2t)] (1+o(1))
      -> 0.

The additional A prefactor is positive because

    1+(x-a)/(2(t+a))=(2t+a+x)/(2(t+a))>0

for t>=0 and x,a in J, and its y/x ratio tends to one. Thus
A_y/A_x -> 0 for x<y, while A_a=1.

If a centered finite combination has zero L2(mu_a) norm, strict positivity of
the density and continuity make its uncentered combination equal to a constant
everywhere. Adding that constant as the A_a coefficient gives an identically
zero finite combination of distinct A_x. Dividing first by the smallest-node
feature and taking t to infinity eliminates its coefficient; finite iteration
eliminates all coefficients. The same argument is valid over the complex
scalars. Therefore

    E_mu |sum_i c_i(A_(x_i)-E_mu A_(x_i))|^2 > 0

for every nonzero complex row at finite distinct non-anchor nodes.

No positivity of S_a, V beyond the already available one-node diagonal, C_V,
or an unconstructed feature space is used in this proof.

